message: "If you use or refer to GCR, please cite it as below. / Pour citer GCR, utilisez la référence ci-dessous."
title: "GCR — Clés RSA à graine rejouable, pour des certificats africains"
abstract: "GCR is a pair of preliminary draft standards and their reference code. GCR-0001 fixes how an RSA key is made: its two primes are built from a seed by a public computation (Shawe-Taylor provable primes, FIPS 186-4), so that the same seed gives the same key with any conforming program and the holder can prove where the key comes from. GCR-0002 states how a certification authority using such keys is created, keeps its keys and issues ordinary X.509 certificates. This repository holds both standards (French reference text and English translation), a Python reference implementation, a second JavaScript implementation, test vectors and a reference authority tool."
